  "title": "DataAccessV1dot9",
  "description": "K-05 v1.9, a minor version of the data-access calls (T-1226, from join 13's round 1 Need 2 and STATE note 38; DL-466; QUESTIONS.md CQ-201). It only adds to v1.8 (data-access.v1.8.schema.json, frozen and unchanged, referred to here, which refers on to v1.7, v1.6, v1.5, v1.4, v1.3, v1.2, v1.1 and v1): every v1.8 definition is here under its own name, the unchanged ones by reference; the changed ones, markPart.response and markPart.exchange, take one new optional field, repeatedDelivery, so every v1 to v1.8 exchange is a v1.9 exchange. Added: markPart's answer to a delivery receipt that repeats one already recorded says what it repeats (README item 48; arch 02 lines 109 and 127): whether that recorded delivery was the row's first (firstOfRow: no other part try of the row holds an earlier K-04 v1 outbox_parts.delivered_at) and when it was delivered (deliveredAt, the delivered_at the part holds), so the caller hands a repeat of the row's first delivery to the clock arming, whose armClock is safe to repeat (README item 5), and a crash between markPart's commit and armClock no longer loses the arming. firstDelivery keeps v1's meaning: the mark that records the row's first delivery says it, and a repeat never does. The call reads only the delivered_at of the row's parts, which it already locks (README item 15), so no column, grant, index or migration is added. A v1.9 call always writes the field: markPart.v1dot9Response is its answer with the field required. Not model-facing, so number and length limits are schema rules here. Owner: the architect.",
